    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and the full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the per-city owner capacity rule: creating an owner whose city already contains 50 or more owners is now rejected with **409 Conflict**.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`OwnerCityFullException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` carrying the offending city, following the pattern of the existing duplicate-owner exceptions.\n\n2. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for `OwnerCityFullException` that returns a 409 `ProblemDetail` with `errors: [\"city\"]`, mirroring the existing conflict handlers.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 added a `CITY_OWNER_LIMIT = 50` constant and a `countOwnersInCity` helper (case-insensitive, consistent with the existing `buildCustomerCode`/`countNamesakes` counting). Before saving, if the city already holds \u2265 50 owners it throws `OwnerCityFullException`. The check sits alongside the existing duplicate-telephone and duplicate-household conflict checks.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` test (fill a fresh city to 50, expect the 51st to 409) passes, and the full suite builds green.",
